Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||06-17-2001||10:52 PM||||I'm making the move....<P>I've just taken pics of my Minolta Maxxum kit (individually) for posting on eBay. This kit has taken me through a lot, from pics of my family to headshots, models' portfolios, and even some advertising and event photography. Even though I want to sell it, there's a part of me that is still attached.<P>Why am I doing this? My style is changing (and my wife isn't too particular to the modelling shoots), less oriented on the business thing (Shooting for money), and more on the fine art stuff. In this vein, I'm going Leica. As a camera (and telescope, and darkroom, and, well, you get the idea) salesperson, Leica has made an offer that I can't refuse, and it looks like I'm destined for an M6 and a 50mm f2.8, a 50 f2, or a 35 f2 (if I get enough for the Maxxum stuff).<P>For those who aren't familiar Maxxum is Minolta Autofocus stuff, and Leica is, well, Leica. It's like owning a decent Japanese car (Say, a Lexus SC400 or a 300ZX Twin Turbo), and moving to a Porsche 911.<P>Anyway, it'll be a few days before I get the images resized, etc. for auction. If anyone here is looking for good photo gear, and you want first shot before they get posted, e-mail me, and I can send the pics. Equipment list as follows:<P>Maxxum 9xi body with Custom Function and Data Memory Cards<BR>Maxxum 8000i body with Custom Function and Data Memory Cards<BR>16mm f2.8 AF with rear cap and Leather "hat"<BR>24mm f2.8 AF with B+W UV and caps<BR>28mm f2.8 AF with B+W UV and rear cap<BR>50mm f1.4 AF with B+W UV and caps<BR>135mm f2.8 AF with B+W UV and caps (front not OEM)<BR>5200i flash with case and Lumiquest Softbox and Pocket Bounce<BR>Wireless Flash Controller (Does not work with 5200i. Was for future expansion)<BR>Short (1') wired remote control.<P>As you can see, I have some $$ invested, but I don't think that's it. The 16mm is part of it, I'm sure. What a beautiful piece of glass.... I keep saying, "I'm getting an M6, I'm getting an M6."||||reg||4
